message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on Type III composite cylinders for compressed gas. The relevant heading is 7311 (containers for compressed or liquefied gas, of iron or steel), but these have an aluminum liner, so heading 7613 (aluminum containers for compressed or liquefied gas) applies. The composite overwrap does not change the classification because the aluminum liner gives the cylinder its essential character.

HTSUS 7613.00.00 is "Aluminum containers for compressed or liquefied gas," and the statistical suffixes are 7613.00.0000 in total, with no further breakouts.

{"hts_code": "7613.00.0000", "reason": "Aluminum-lined cylinders for storing high-pressure gas are aluminum containers for compressed or liquefied gas of heading 7613, with the aluminum liner giving the essential character despite the carbon fiber/epoxy overwrap."}
